; case: invalid-contradictory-presence
; expect: invalid-description
; why: One declaration says a fact is both offered and absent. §5.3: reject contradictory declarations
;   rather than choosing one. A contradiction is one declaration's: two blocks, one offering a fact and
;   one declaring it absent, are two devices' two statements, each judged on its own (model §2 rule 1;
;   docs/decisions/decision_absence-per-provider.md, leaf M3.4.8, which rewrote this case from that
;   two-block spelling — docs/semantics/migrations/eadl-1-an-absence-is-a-declaration-s-statement.md).
;
(eadl-version eadl/1)

(defblock a (offers low-power-timer) (absent low-power-timer))
(defblock b (offers x))
